    {
      "id": "lombok-lesson-2",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Constructor injection with Lombok"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lombok-lesson-2-example-0",
      "type": "example",
      "example": {
        "title": "Generate a constructor for a service dependency",
        "language": "java",
        "description": [
          "Java `17` and Maven are required. The files form a separate project rooted at `pom.xml`.",
          "Java `17` discovers the Lombok annotation processor from the dependency. The IDE also needs Lombok support to recognize generated members."
        ],
        "code": "",
        "explanation": [
          "Lombok generates `EntryService(TitlePolicy titlePolicy)` during compilation.",
          "`@Service` registers the class with Spring. Spring calls its single constructor and supplies the `TitlePolicy` bean.",
          "`@RequiredArgsConstructor` supplies the constructor. It does not create the dependency or perform injection.",
          "`prepareTitle(\"  First entry  \")` returns `First entry`."
        ],
        "commands": "mvn clean package",
        "files": [
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/TitlePolicy.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.springframework.stereotype.Component;\n\n@Component\npublic class TitlePolicy {\n    public String normalize(String title) {\n        return title.strip();\n    }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/EntryService.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport lombok.RequiredArgsConstructor;\nimport org.springframework.stereotype.Service;\n\n@Service\n@RequiredArgsConstructor\npublic class EntryService {\n    private final TitlePolicy titlePolicy;\n\n    public String prepareTitle(String title) {\n        return titlePolicy.normalize(title);\n    }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/DemoApplication.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;\nimport org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;\n\n@SpringBootApplication\npublic class DemoApplication {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        SpringApplication.run(DemoApplication.class, args);\n    }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "pom.xml",
            "language": "text",
            "code": "<project xmlns=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\"\n         xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd\">\n    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>\n    <parent>\n        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>\n        <version>3.5.16</version>\n        <relativePath/>\n    </parent>\n    <groupId>com.example</groupId>\n    <artifactId>demo</artifactId>\n    <version>1.0.0</version>\n    <properties><java.version>17</java.version></properties>\n    <dependencies>\n        <dependency>\n            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>\n        </dependency>\n        <dependency>\n            <groupId>org.projectlombok</groupId>\n            <artifactId>lombok</artifactId>\n            <optional>true</optional>\n        </dependency>\n    </dependencies>\n    <build>\n        <finalName>demo</finalName>\n        <plugins>\n            <plugin>\n                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n                <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>\n            </plugin>\n        </plugins>\n    </build>\n\n</project>\n"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lombok-lesson-3",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Data classes and entities"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lombok-lesson-3-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@Data",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " does not promise both a no-argument constructor and an all-arguments constructor."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lombok-lesson-3-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@NonNull",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " on an uninitialized field makes it a required constructor argument. Lombok also generates a null check for that argument."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lombok-lesson-3-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Generated setters allow callers to change fields. Generated equality depends on the selected fields."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lombok-lesson-3-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Generated "
        ],
        [
          "toString",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " can print private fields. "
        ],
        [
          "@ToString.Exclude",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " leaves a field out."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lombok-lesson-3-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A JPA entity needs a public or protected no-argument constructor, as covered in the relational-data notes."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lombok-lesson-3-note-5",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "JPA relationships can cause recursive "
        ],
        [
          "toString",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " calls or unexpected lazy loading. Their fields need deliberate inclusion or exclusion."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lombok-lesson-3-note-6",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Lombok does not replace Jackson mapping or Bean Validation annotations."
        ]
      ]
    }
